wave3-firmware office checks, 2026-10-07 (branch fix/wave3-firmware, HEAD rebased onto main d99a0ff)

Setup: phone hotspot, Mac and device on the same subnet (2.4 GHz, channel 6), live backend = main's server image
(container TZ=Europe/Dublin; its OTA reply carries server_time.timezone_offset=60 and no `tz`, because main's image
has no weixue_clock overlay). Device USB-powered, nobody instructed to touch it. Audio and wake checks: SKIPPED (office mode).
Device lock: taken with scripts/device_lock.sh acquire (09:08:54Z), held through the flash, both captures and the
main reflash, released after the reflash. SSID, BSSID, MACs and IPs are redacted below (<WIFI_SSID>, <mac>, <ip>).

Builds (firmware/build.sh, provenance checked by flash.sh):
  diag   WEIXUE_FACE_DIAG=1 on the branch: xiaozhi.bin 3,054,384 B, 131 s, flash.sh OK (full 32 MB MAC-tagged backup verified)
  main   release at d99a0ff: xiaozhi.bin 3,040,608 B, flash.sh OK; boot below shows no diag lines
  host tests (firmware/tests/run.sh): imu_gestures, ring_bedside, clock, session = OK (115 PASS lines); 23 python tests OK

RESULTS
(a) Clock / TZ
  PASS  device local time = Europe/Dublin: diag screen dumps show the status-bar clock 10:12 (dump 2, 92 s after reset,
        09:12Z) and 10:16 (dump 7, 343 s, 09:16Z), i.e. UTC+1.
  N/A   `Clock: TZ ...` / `Clock: stored TZ ...` lines: not logged, the live server sends timezone_offset, not a POSIX tz
        (that branch of patch 27 is the "adds timezone_offset as before" path and logs nothing).
  NOT EXERCISED  `Clock: resynced from the backend Date header`: no drift of 2 s or more occurred in 450 s + 330 s,
        so the line is correctly absent; no way to induce drift without changing the server.
(b) Panel taps (virtual pointer replay at 42 s and every 120 s: swipe left, Approve, Deny, swipe right)
  backend reachable (run 1, 46.6 s and 54.7 s; run 2, 46.6 s and 54.7 s; repeated at 286 s and 406 s):
        `Device event sent (own session)` 0.57 s (Approve) and 0.61 s (Deny) after the tap.
  server paused (docker pause 09:13:21Z, unpause 09:13:41Z = run 1 163 s to 183 s):
    PASS  Approve tap at 166.588 s: handler returned at once, card went to sending; `Device event not sent (timeout)` at
          170.588 s (4.00 s, the documented limit). Deny tap at 174.738 s: `not sent (busy)` logged in the same
          millisecond (the first event's own session was still waiting; `WebSocket handshake timeout` at 176.608 s).
    PASS  no error chime or alert: no Alert/Play/sound line and no `mode=` change in the window; `SystemInfo` heap line kept its
          10 s period (164.278, 174.278, 184.278) and the face timer kept logging through the pause.
    FAIL against the expected outcome "row shows checking, not offline, after unpause": the row stayed `online` (stale, <90 s)
          until the proactive poll that was in flight during the pause hit the device's 40 s header timeout:
          `Proactive poll failed (status 0)` at 203.998 s -> `diag backend=offline poll_status=0 poll_age_ms=62` at
          204.058 s (21 s after the unpause), then `diag backend=online poll_status=204` at 235.548 s (next poll).
          `checking` never appeared after the pause. BackendRowFor returns `checking` only for a failed poll from before a
          session or mute resume (`polled_since_resume` false); a poll that fails while the server is paused is `offline` by
          that rule. `checking` appeared at boot (`diag backend=checking poll_status=0 poll_age_ms=-1`, 3.1 s) until the first poll.
(c) IMU driver (diag build injects a 120 ms stall + extra read every 30 s and a read failure every 45 s)
  PASS  counters present: `IMU diag: overruns=.. resyncs=.. skipped=.. read_errors=.. torn_timestamps=..` and
        `IMU resync after N ms without a sample (n)`. Run 1 at 422 s: overruns=25 resyncs=20 skipped=40 read_errors=9
        torn_timestamps=2; run 2 at 317 s: overruns=21 resyncs=15 skipped=31 read_errors=6 torn_timestamps=2. Every injected
        stall or failure gave one resync; torn timestamp reads were corrected by the re-read (no extra resync).
  PASS  run 2 (reset boot, untouched, 330 s): 0 `IMU gesture:` lines.
  NOTE  run 1 logged one `IMU gesture: pick_up (count 1)` at 24.9 s after reset, none in the following 337 s of idle
        (30 s to 362 s, with the injected stalls every 30 s and read failures every 45 s). Run 1 also shows a touch wake (`Panel on` at 362.8 s,
        no IMU gesture) and manual panel swipes at 365 s and 369 s, so a person was at the device; the pick_up at 24.9 s did not
        recur in run 2 (same boot, same time window) and is attributed to handling, not to the driver.
(d) Mute invariant, static evidence only (no hands, no gesture, no audio)
  firmware/patches/24-application-mute-transport.patch: MuteFence::SendMicAudio gates every microphone send,
  AcceptTtsStart/AcceptTtsStop drop tts messages scheduled before a mute (generation counter), StartListening closes the
  channel instead of listening while muted, SetMicMuted(true) -> ActionsOnMute closes the transport whatever its state.
  Host tests (session_test) PASS: tts start/stop from before a mute dropped (also after unmute), tts start refused while
  muted, no microphone audio sent while muted, listening refused while muted, mute closes a timed-out channel's transport,
  mute in a session returns to idle, mute while speaking aborts + closes + idles, mute while idle still closes the transport.
  Not run on device this session (needs a physical face-down or the diag MCP tool through a conversation).

Skipped: all audio, wake-word, TTS and conversation checks; physical gesture trials.

Reflash: main firmware (d99a0ff) flashed with firmware/flash.sh; reset boot reaches idle, Wi-Fi and OTA ok, proactive poller
started, no `diag` lines (see the last section).

